@page "/events/data-point-selection"

<DocExamples Title="Data Point Selection">

    <Description>
        <p>Click on a datapoint to trigger the event</p>
        <p>
            On line, area and radar charts the click has to land on a marker, so when <code>OnDataPointSelection</code> or <code>OnDataPointEnter</code> is set
            the chart shows markers (size 5 when none is set) and switches the tooltip to <code>Intersect = true</code>, <code>Shared = false</code>.
            In that mode the tooltip and the event describe one series: the marker under the cursor. When several series have the same value at the same point,
            only the marker drawn on top is reported.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you need every series at the clicked point, use <code>OnMarkerClick</code> or <code>OnClick</code> instead. They keep the shared tooltip, which lists
            all series, and <code>DataPointIndex</code> tells you which x value was clicked, so you can read each series' data point at that index.
        </p>
    </Description>

